          "filename": "Sea King Helicopter near Hemmel House - geograph.org.uk - 1608241.jpg",
          "caption": "Sea King Helicopter near Hemmel House RAF Boulmer is less than 1.5 miles as the crow/helicopter flies from where the photo was taken. It is a frequent sight to see the Sea Kings coming into land in this area from various directions.  They always look impressive especially the one we saw many years ago hovering over Cullernose Point facing into the wind and being held in the same position for about 10 minutes.  It wheeled away and headed back home.",
